{
  "dom_id": "questionContainer",
  "name": "Question 66",
  "problem": "Peter has $8$ shirts, $6$ pants, and $6$ pairs of shoes. If Peter wears one shirt, one pant, and one pair of shoes, how many different ways can Peter dress?",
  "worked_solution": "Using the **rule of product**, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Number of outfits} & =\\text{Number of shirts} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of pants} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of pairs of shoes} \\\\  & =8\\times 6\\times 6 \\\\  & =288.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Peter can dress in $288$ different ways.",
